WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.062
Let us finish Module 4 by connecting the major ideas
First grain

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:10.200
comes before GROUP BY syntax Always know what one
output row represents

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:16.488
Second NULL matters COUNT star counts rows while
COUNT column counts non-NULL

00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:21.438
values AVG and other aggregates can also be affected
by missing values

00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:26.675
and by the population you choose Third filtering
happens at different stages

00:00:27.562 --> 00:00:33.088
WHERE removes source rows before grouping HAVING
removes completed groups after aggregate

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:39.100
values exist Fourth conditional aggregation lets one
grouped row contain several metrics

00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:44.350
CASE is flexible and portable while PostgreSQL
FILTER is often concise and

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:49.625
readable Fifth GROUPING SETS ROLLUP and CUBE can
place several summary grains

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:55.262
in one result GROUPING helps label subtotal rows
correctly Finally

00:00:55.462 --> 00:01:00.762
window functions add analytical context without
collapsing the detail rows You used

00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:06.112
them for ranking group averages company averages and
running totals The larger

00:01:06.138 --> 00:01:09.675
lesson is a workflow ask a clear question define the
grain choose

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.712
meaningful measures filter at the correct stage and
validate the result Those

00:01:14.738 --> 00:01:18.112
habits will support the more advanced SQL topics
that come next
